# C050 — a REGISTRY-DISTRIBUTED SaaS-backend framework (architecture-only; operator chose "record it, build later").
# Operator realization: ~30 of toolfactory's ~33 api/src modules are GENERIC backend plumbing (auth/keys/credits/billing/
# cost/logs/rate-limit/erasure/stores/audit/journeys); only whisper.ts + lib/subtitle/ + the transcribe/convert routes are
# the product. Vision: a framework set up ONCE, that provisions real backend services via OSB (@suluk/provision) and
# DOWNLOADS modules into a repo via the shadcn GitHub registry (single `shadcn add` command). NOT a contract facet.

# THREE COMPOSABLE LAYERS: @suluk/* (npm) = the LOGIC (credits atomic ledger, keys pooled-cap, payments, cost, harden,
# journeys) + a shadcn REGISTRY = the OWNED WIRING (per-module routes+schema-fragment+Hono glue, copied in via
# `shadcn add <user>/<repo>/<item>` — reads registry.json from the repo, no server; files carry `target` paths so backend
# code lands anywhere; + npm dependencies + registryDependencies chaining + envVars + `#ref` pinning) + @suluk/provision
# (OSB) = the INFRA (each item ships a PROVISION FRAGMENT = InstanceSpec[] merged into provision.config.ts; generate/
# migrate creates D1/KV/connector). COMPOSITION = HYBRID (operator decision): items OWN the wiring but DEP the @suluk
# package for money/security-critical logic, so a correctness fix (atomic-debit CAS / pooled cap / idempotent grant /
# Stripe status-map) flows to EVERY consumer via npm while the app owns its editable surface — money logic must NOT fork
# per repo. ~10 items over ~30 files (app/auth/keys/credits/billing/cost/logs/stores/erasure/audit/journeys). Setup-once
# flow: shadcn add the modules (regDeps chain the order) -> provision apply -> write only the product routes.
claim registry_framework_three_layers_hybrid_shadcn_osb_npm: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when registry_framework_three_layers_hybrid_shadcn_osb_npm == False

# C050 REFRAMES C049 + honest CAVEATS. The toolfactory "adoption" (C049) becomes EXTRACTION: turning its generic modules
# into registry items IS the generalization; toolfactory then becomes ONE CONSUMER of the registry; C049's phases (A audit
# -> B provision -> C money) become the EXTRACTION ORDER (money modules last, parity-tested, thin-wiring-over-npm never
# forked). TWO FEASIBILITY CAVEATS a single-module PoC (credits) MUST close before extracting the rest: (1) the plain
# user/repo/item GitHub form is PUBLIC-ONLY — a private Suluk registry needs shadcn's namespace+authentication; (2) DB
# schema/migrations aren't a native registry concept — each item ships a schema FRAGMENT file + a provision fragment and
# @suluk/provision owns table creation; a backend target also needs a minimal components.json (or absolute target paths).
# Naming + the registry's home repo are OPEN. Backend-first; a web/UI registry (toolfactory web/) is a natural Phase 2 +
# the shadcn sweet spot. DESIGNED-not-built => ceiling 0.5.
claim registry_framework_reframes_c049_extraction_with_poc_caveats: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when registry_framework_reframes_c049_extraction_with_poc_caveats == False

# C050 BUILD #1 — the shadcn registry + first vertical slice built 2026-07-01 (operator: "add a registry to this repo"
# [shadcn github registry] + "provision effect ts services like toolfactory's auth/billing/credits"). registry.json at the
# REPO ROOT (public repo MahmoodKhalil57/suluk -> the plain `shadcn add MahmoodKhalil57/suluk/<item>` form works, no
# namespace/auth). Two items: `app` (base Hono app + the Effect-TS `Db` service — Context.Tag + DbLive(env) Layer from the
# D1 binding) + `credits` (registryDep app; the HYBRID demonstrator). FINDING (honest): toolfactory does NOT use Effect
# SERVICES — no Context.Tag/Layer/Effect.Service anywhere; only Effect.Schema+Either in billing.ts. So there was no
# existing service pattern to copy; the registry modules are made PROPER Effect services (a strict upgrade matching the
# operator's intent), wrapping the @suluk/* plain-function logic: credits.service.ts = `class Credits extends Context.Tag`
# + `CreditsLive = Layer.effect(...Effect.gen -> Db, wraps getBalance/debitIfCovers/grantOnce/listTransactions)`;
# credits.routes.ts = Hono handlers that Effect.provide(CreditsLive, DbLive(env)) + runPromise; credits.schema.ts re-
# exports @suluk/credits tables; credits.provision.ts = the InstanceSpec[] fragment (shared d1 ref "db", protected, the
# credit_* migration). HYBRID RULE intact: own the Effect service wiring, npm the money-critical logic (atomic CAS +
# idempotent grant stay in @suluk/credits so fixes flow). VALIDATED: registry.json valid JSON + all file paths exist; all
# 5 TS files transpile clean; `bunx shadcn build` SUCCEEDED ("Building app... Building credits... done") — structurally
# shadcn-consumable. Generated public/r/ gitignored (github form reads registry.json directly). NOT pushed yet (shadcn add
# needs the commit on the public repo). REMAINING: push; then the generator/manifest (C051) + the other ~8 modules.
claim registry_c050_build1_shadcn_registry_credits_effect_service_validated: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build1_shadcn_registry_credits_effect_service_validated == False

