# C050 BUILD #3 — the `auth` FOUNDATION module built 2026-07-01 (the coupled Better-Auth mount, given its own careful pass).
# auth.ts: buildAuth (betterAuth config — drizzleAdapter(sqlite,schema) + plugins openAPI/apiKey/passkey, parametrized
# secret/baseURL/trustedOrigins/optional-google + an optional onUserCreated hook = the auth<->credits signup-grant seam) +
# createAuth (WeakMap-cached per DB binding) + mountAuthRoutes (app.on GET/POST /api/auth/* -> createAuth(c.env).handler,
# the correct per-request pattern — NOT @suluk/better-auth mountAuth which wants a static handler) + a CurrentUser Effect
# service (Context.Tag + currentUserLayer(env,headers) via api.getSession). auth.schema.ts: the Better-Auth-v1 tables
# (user/session/account/verification + apikey + passkey) — HONESTLY MARKED A SCAFFOLD (canonical = `@better-auth/cli
# generate`; the apikey table is what keys' cascade-revoke soft-disables enabled=0). auth.provision.ts: the 6-table
# migration (0000_auth, FIRST — the user table others reference), scaffold-flagged. registryDeps app; deps better-auth +
# @better-auth/api-key + @better-auth/passkey + @suluk/provision + effect + hono + drizzle-orm. keys registryDep now +auth
# (needs the apikey table). Registry now 6 items = a COHERENT SaaS backend CORE (app/auth/credits/keys/billing/logs).
# VALIDATED: registry.json 6 items all-paths-exist; auth TS transpiles; `bunx shadcn build` SUCCEEDED for all 6. HONESTY:
# Better Auth's schema is CLI-generated + version/plugin-dependent, so auth ships the correct config/mount/CurrentUser
# (reusable) + a schema SCAFFOLD to reconcile — not byte-exact. REMAINING for the one-shot: optionally cost/journeys/audit,
# then the C051 manifest generator, then generate autotoolfactory + diff-parity vs toolfactory.
claim registry_c050_build3_auth_foundation_module_scaffold_schema_validated: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build3_auth_foundation_module_scaffold_schema_validated == False

# C050 BUILD #4 — the REMAINING modules + AUTH RECONCILE + a measured parity-diff (2026-07-01; operator: "do diff-parity,
# remaining modules and auth"). PARITY-DIFF (5 Explore agents over autotoolfactory-vs-toolfactory): registry COVERS 6
# concerns (auth/credits/keys/billing/logs + now cost), PARTIAL on 3 (mcp-oauth caps, gdpr-cascade, middleware-debit — all
# app-specific glue), MISSING product-specific 2 (whisper transcription + subtitle-convert = the deliberately-excluded
# product routes), and the non-product gaps are dev/CI tooling now filled by journeys+audit + app-glue the generated app
# owns. THREE NEW MODULES built to the established pattern: (1) `cost` — a RUNTIME Effect service over @suluk/cost (the
# storage-agnostic µ$ algebra: summarize/principalCost projections + eventCostEvent attribution/dedupe stay upstream);
# OWNS the cost_event + cost_dedup D1 tables; record (live-request sink) + recordEvent (fired background event, deduped via
# a single-statement onConflictDoNothing().returning() claim = at-least-once safe) + summary/principalSummary; routes GET
# /cost/summary[/:userId] + POST /event + POST /dedup; provision fragment 0003_cost. (2) `journeys` — DEV-FILES (no runtime
# mount): journeys.config + example.feature + a bun:test coverage harness (parseFeature+generateVocabulary+bindFeatures+
# coverageGrade over @suluk/journeys; test.skipIf(no-contract) so a fresh platform is green). (3) `audit` — DEV-FILES: one
# scripts/conformance.ts CI gate consolidating cockpit conformanceGates/shipSummary + harden auditDocument/auditReadiness/
# combineGrades into a single pass/fail with a grade floor. AUTH RECONCILED to Better Auth v1.6.23 (canonical, extracted
# from installed node_modules — NOT a guess): apikey gains configId + referenceId (v1.6 api-key plugin REQUIRES them),
# rateLimitEnabled default flipped FALSE->TRUE(1) + rateLimitTimeWindow=60 + rateLimitMax=10, verification createdAt/
# updatedAt now NOT NULL, + the 5 plugin indexes (apikey configId/referenceId/key, passkey userId/credentialID) in BOTH
# the drizzle schema AND the provision SQL. So auth is no longer a "scaffold" guess — it's version-pinned canonical.
# CATALOG got a new "dev" Mount kind (files-only: no entry mount, no provision fragment) so journeys/audit generate as
# tooling. Registry now 9 items (app/auth/credits/keys/billing/cost/logs/journeys/audit). VALIDATED: platform 9 pass
# (added cost-route + dev-mount assertions); `bunx shadcn build` SUCCEEDED for all 9; all 9 new/changed files transpile;
# all new npm deps live (cost 0.2.0/journeys 0.4.0/cockpit 0.2.0/harden 0.2.0/core 0.1.13) so autotoolfactory can install.
claim registry_c050_build4_cost_journeys_audit_modules_auth_reconciled_parity_measured: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build4_cost_journeys_audit_modules_auth_reconciled_parity_measured == False

# C050 BUILD #5 — the `erasure` module (GDPR account-erasure), 2026-07-01. Closes the parity report's erasure-gdpr PARTIAL
# gap with a proper HYBRID module (the pattern held): npm the fail-closed ORCHESTRATOR (@suluk/better-auth's
# beforeDeleteCascade — if a cleanup step throws it ABORTS rather than half-erasing then deleting the user, so a fix flows
# via npm), OWN the wiring. erasure.service.ts: an Effect `Erasure` service (erase = run the cascade then write the
# receipt) + `sulukCascade(db)` = ordered leaf-first deleteSteps over the core Suluk tables (activity_log, cost_event,
# billing_account, key_lineage, credit_transaction — ALL key on userId, verified) via parameterized `sql`DELETE FROM
# ${sql.identifier(table)} WHERE userId = ${id}`` + `erasureHook(db)` (the Better Auth deleteUser.beforeDelete builder,
# the PROPER integration) + re-exported step/anonymizeStep constructors (the app PICKS the posture delete-vs-anonymize +
# TRIMS the cascade to installed modules). erasure.schema.ts: an OWNED erasure_receipt GDPR audit table (id/userId/posture/
# steps-JSON/erasedAt), written only AFTER the cascade succeeds (a failed/aborted erase leaves NO false "erased" record).
# erasure.routes.ts: POST /erasure/:userId (admin-gate in prod). erasure.provision.ts: 0004_erasure. registryDep app only
# (the cascade hits other modules' tables by NAME in raw SQL, no code import → decoupled; a missing table fails-closed as
# designed). @suluk/platform catalog got the erasure route entry; platform tests 10 pass (added the /erasure route +
# provision-merge assertion). Registry now 10 ITEMS. VALIDATED: 4 erasure TS transpile; `bunx shadcn build` ok all 10;
# platform 10 pass. CLEAN-ROOM PROOF (end-to-end, without touching autotoolfactory or republishing platform): a FRESH temp
# project `shadcn add MahmoodKhalil57/suluk/erasure` pulled 5 files (erasure + app via registryDep), bun install + tsc = 0
# own-code errors (the lone error is the pre-existing @suluk/openapi-compat transitive nit). FINDING: shadcn lands targets
# at ROOT (not src/) when the project has no pre-existing src/ dir — the whole tree shifts uniformly so relative imports
# still resolve. Shipped as a LIVE registry module (pushed); the @suluk/platform 0.1.2 republish + autotoolfactory adoption
# is the batch-cadence follow-up (preserves the build-#4 one-shot-from-installed-generator invariant).
claim registry_c050_build5_erasure_gdpr_cascade_module_cleanroom_proven: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when registry_c050_build5_erasure_gdpr_cascade_module_cleanroom_proven == False
